# Credentials for the agent system — TEMPLATE.
#
# Copy to `config/secrets.env`, remove the `#` in front of the entries for the
# services you use and enter the real value:
#     cp config/secrets.env.example config/secrets.env
# `config/secrets.env` is git-ignored; only this template is tracked.
# The entries are commented out because a placeholder like `sk-or-v1-...`
# counts as a set value: it would only surface as a 401 from the provider
# instead of a "missing" warning at load time (see below).
#
# Format: KEY=value, one line per entry. Quotes are optional, lines starting
# with `#` are comments. No shell escaping — the value is taken as written
# (an API key is an opaque string).
#
# The file is read when the config is loaded. The YAMLs reference the values
# as ${VARIABLE}; a real environment variable always WINS over this file. So a
# server can be configured via systemd/CI without any secrets.env, and a stale
# developer file on the same machine cannot silently replace the server's
# credentials.
#
# A missing entry is warned about by NAME at load time. It does not silently
# become an empty string that shows up hours later as a cryptic 401 from the
# provider.

# --- LLM providers (config/llm.yaml, config/llm_openrouter.yaml) ------------

# OpenRouter — by far the most used access: GPT, Claude, Gemini, DeepSeek,
# Grok, MiniMax, GLM, Kimi, Llama.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# OpenAI direct (Responses API and httpx route).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-...

# TypeSafe direct — only for decision models with `provider: systemone_decisions`
# without their own `url`; Jev via OpenRouter does not need it.
# TYPESAFE_API_KEY=

# Anthropic direct.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# Google Gemini direct — also used for the TTS models and the batch providers.
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...

# DeepSeek direct (OpenAI-compatible, api.deepseek.com).
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Plugins (config/plugins.yaml) ------------------------------------------

# Tavily web search (plugin `tavily_search`).
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-...

# --- External MCP servers (config/mcp_servers.yaml) -------------------------
# The Smithery gateway hosts several of the listed MCP servers; key and profile
# are passed there as query parameters in the URL.
# SMITHERY_API_KEY=...
# SMITHERY_PROFILE=...

# X/Twitter credentials for the x_tools server.
# X_BEARER_TOKEN=...
# X_ACCESS_TOKEN=...
